// Fixture for the `oskel build` native-fn error test (tests/build_error.cmake).
//
// `clock` is a `native fn` the development VM resolves through its host registry
// (a host builtin), so this program runs on the VM. The AOT backend has no host,
// and `clock` has no curated stub, so `oskel build` must fail with the dedicated
// message instead of the generic unassigned-global one a typo produces.
native fn clock(): double;
print(clock());
